"""The frozen v2 visual rubric shared by the two Luna APIs."""
RUBRIC=('Assess visible tyre condition, not physical depth or legal safety. First examine what is actually visible: '
'groove relief and rubber between grooves, wear across the tread face, surface cracking, exposed cords or torn rubber. '
'Distinguish tread DESIGN from CONDITION: the existence of longitudinal lines, zigzags or lugs alone does not prove good condition. '
'Look for raised tread edges and recessed grooves versus broad smooth flattened rubber, faint shallow remnants or locally bald/worn areas. '
'Do not demand a millimetre measurement or a visible TWI to judge visual wear. '
'Mud, shadows and highlights can hide grooves or mimic cracks; do not invent concealed detail or equate dirt with damage. '
'Then classify: bad if clear flattened/bald/shallow-looking wear or visible cracking, cords, tears or severe damage is present. '
'Clear bad evidence is sufficient even when only part of the tyre is visible. '
'good if enough tread face shows distinct groove/raised relief without clear wear or damage; this is only a visual screen. '
'review if only sidewall/rim is shown without clear damage, tread detail is obscured, or wear evidence genuinely conflicts. '
'A partial but clear tread face can suffice; do not automatically reject oblique views. '
'No measured depth, TWI verification, hidden condition or roadworthiness claims. Judge this image alone.')
